Report the mounting user as owner of entries listed via GetObjectPropertyList.

GetObjectInfo sets st_uid/st_gid, but it only populates the storage root. Every
directory below it is filled from GetObjectPropertyList, whose callbacks never
set them, so those entries reported root:wheel. Linux mounts without
default_permissions and never notices; macFUSE enforces ownership, so after a
remount creating, deleting or renaming anything inside an existing subfolder
(DCIM/Camera, for example) failed with EACCES.

--- a/fuse/fuse.cpp
+++ b/fuse/fuse.cpp
@@ -291,6 +291,10 @@
 						{
 							struct stat & attr = _objectAttrs[objectId];
 							attr.st_ino = ToFuse(objectId).Inode;
+							//! GetObjectInfo fills these for the storage root; without them every entry
+							//! below it reports root:wheel, and macFUSE refuses writes by the mounting user.
+							attr.st_uid = getuid();
+							attr.st_gid = getgid();
 							attr.st_mode = FuseEntry::GetMode(format);
 							attr.st_nlink = 1;
 						});
